[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2638188964","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102108#issuecomment-2638188964","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102108","id":2638188964,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dP5Gk","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-05T22:33:04Z","updated_at":"2025-02-05T22:33:04Z","body":"I tried to reproduce the issue on Linux with scenes from the 2D platformer demo in 4.4.beta2 but didn't get any crash.\n\nIt might be system specific, or scene specific. Is your scene particularly complex or using some specific node types which might be relevant?\n\nThe crash trace is a bit confusing, `SceneTreeEditor::_update_tree(bool) + 500` (if 500 is the line number) seems to be an empty line in `_update_node`, while `_update_tree` is much further down.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2638188964/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2638257526","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102108#issuecomment-2638257526","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102108","id":2638257526,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dQJ12","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-05T23:22:11Z","updated_at":"2025-02-06T01:38:54Z","body":"The 500 is in this case the function address offset. I agree the trace is weird though as it shows a get_parent call from _update_tree, which unless I missed something does not happen and I'm not sure what intermediary call might've been inlined to allow that. I don't remember exactly what conditions or versions I tested, and it might be system specific although I tested it in a pretty barebones scene before. I'll test again with beta2 on mac/linux/windows and see what comes up (also I'll change my lldb output format to maybe be clearer lol)\n\nEdit: I'm able to consistently reproduce this on macos in beta1 and beta2, both standard and mono, for scenes containing an AnimationPlayer, although re \"consistently\" I'm pretty sure it's a race condition somewhere as sometimes the crash happens on 1st interaction and sometimes it takes like a minute of spam open/closing the scene and clicking randomly on nodes. I'm going to try to repro on windows + linux and then see if I can get a better trace.\n\n[glb_test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18680946/glb_test.zip)\n\nEdit 2: I was able to repro on Windows although it was waaaaay less likely than on the macbook. I was only able to get it to crash twice, both times with `STATUS_HEAP_CORRUPTION`. I only tested beta2 standard since on the macbook it didn't seem to matter.\n\nEdit 3: And I'm also able to repro on my older linux laptop also with beta2 pretty easily with SIGSEGV, although the info I get in console is completely useless.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2638257526/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2638985937","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102108#issuecomment-2638985937","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102108","id":2638985937,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dS7rR","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-06T06:56:33Z","updated_at":"2025-02-06T07:56:49Z","body":"Good news(?) it does actually happen with debugging stuff enabled, I just was unlucky when previously testing it. Looks like maybe there's a race to update the pinned node and it can end up stale in certain cases:\n```\n[3] SceneTreeEditor::NodeCache::mark_dirty(Node*, bool) (in godot.macos.editor.dev.arm64.mono) (/Users/adam/code/godot/editor/gui/scene_tree_editor.cpp:2420)\n[4] SceneTreeEditor::_update_tree(bool) (in godot.macos.editor.dev.arm64.mono) (/Users/adam/code/godot/editor/gui/scene_tree_editor.cpp:932)\n```\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/editor/gui/scene_tree_editor.cpp#L932\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/editor/gui/scene_tree_editor.cpp#L2420\n\nIt sorta makes sense that I didn't run into this when testing the original pr before (besides the crash being sorta rare) since I was mostly using the test scene with thousands of empty base nodes and no AnimationPlayer. At worst, the mark dirty could check for instance validity rather than null but I'll try looking for a nicer solution.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2638985937/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2639824023","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102108#issuecomment-2639824023","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102108","id":2639824023,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dWISX","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-06T13:25:02Z","updated_at":"2025-02-06T13:25:02Z","body":"Thank you for the great report and the digging!\n\nI want to have a look to see how a node actually gets in that state in the editor. It might need a different signal being handled. If a \"bad node\" can make it into that codepath then it would cause problems elsewhere as well, in code I didn't even touch.\n\nThis might have been a preexisting issue that was just even more rare before.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2639824023/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2640824822","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102108#issuecomment-2640824822","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102108","id":2640824822,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dZ8n2","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-06T19:38:10Z","updated_at":"2025-02-06T20:11:18Z","body":"Maybe there's a different triggering condition but the only thing I can think of is that the only time `current_pinned_node` is set is 1) if there's a current root node and 2) if the current pin is different from the previous pin, so the old pin always sticks around and if that node has already been freed the crash occurs. My first thought was just to reset all the fields in `node_cache.clear()`, so it would always be nulled when the edited scene changes, but that didn't work. I think since the old code updated the full tree each time it would be unlikely that this same crash could happen.\n\nEdit: ok I _did_ notice before while doing repro that I very rarely got a different offset and now it looks like `AnimationPlayerEditor::get_editing_node()` can actually give back an already freed node. So either it's freed by the time the the tree updates and it crashes or it's freed by the next time the tree updates and it crashes. Clearing the cache on the tree being reset only covers the second case.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2640824822/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2642838057","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102108#issuecomment-2642838057","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102108","id":2642838057,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dhoIp","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb","html_url":"https://github.com/hpvb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hpvb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-07T12:55:06Z","updated_at":"2025-02-07T12:55:06Z","body":"I understand what needs to happen, a PR is incoming! I'm on a trip this weekend so it might not be until Monday.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2642838057/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2644238697","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/102108#issuecomment-2644238697","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102108","id":2644238697,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dm-Fp","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-07T22:24:13Z","updated_at":"2025-02-07T22:24:13Z","body":"Were you able to repro or were you going off of my description/stack trace? My impression was we needed to both clear the cache values when the tree was cleared and also update the AnimationPlayerEditor to clear its editing node when the scene was changed as well, but I wasn't sure of a good mechanism for the latter.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2644238697/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-